          %h2#InQuantumProbability In quantum probability theory
          %p
            In the dual algebraic formulation of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/probability+theory"} probability theory
            known as
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/noncommutative+probability+theory"} noncommutative probability theory
            or
            = succeed "," do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quantum+probability+theory"} quantum probability theory
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/expectation+value"} expectation value
            is primitive (while that of the corresponding
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/probability+space"} probability space
            (if it exists) is a derived concept), the concept of conditional expection appears as follows (e.g.
            = succeed "):" do
              %a{:href => "#RedeiSummers06"} Redei-Summers 06, section 7.3
          %p
            Let
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi 𝒜
                  %mo ,
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ⟨
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ⟩
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\mathcal{A},\langle -\rangle)
            be a
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quantum+probability+space"} quantum probability space
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/complex+numbers"} complex
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/star+algebra"} star algebra
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi 𝒜
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{A}
            of
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quantum+observables"} quantum observables
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/state+on+a+star-algebra"} state on a star-algebra
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ⟨
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ⟩
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
